I see an opportunity to Copilot as a proactive support channel for IDIRA issues (SIA, SWS, PSM..) etc.  enabling users to resolve common issues independently before resorting to opening an Incident. By integrating our existing Knowledge Base content and known issue repositories into an intelligent chatbot, we can provide instant access to relevant troubleshooting guidance and proven solutions.
 
Rather than requiring users to navigate the ServiceNow Knowledge Base, an AI-powered Copilot agent could serve as a single point of engagement, providing instant access to known issues, troubleshooting guidance, and knowledge articles. This would empower users to resolve common issues independently, reduce incident volumes, improve time-to-resolution, and increase adoption of existing knowledge assets.
 
Copilot Studio agent could be trained on KB articles, known issues, FAQs, and operational procedures, then integrated into Teams or a web portal so users can get answers before opening an INC.
 
User
  ↓
Microsoft Teams / Web Portal
  ↓
Copilot Studio Agent
  ↓
Knowledge Sources
   ├─ ServiceNow KB Articles
   ├─ Known Issues Database
   ├─ CyberArk Runbooks
   ├─ SOP Documents
   ├─ SharePoint Knowledge Libraries
   └─ FAQs
  ↓
Response to User
 
If unresolved
  ↓
Create Incident in ServiceNow
 
These agent can be deployed to Team as an icon, Called (PAM Support Copilot Agent).
 
So the Teams copilot agent will help point users to the suitable KB
